# Money Care FE Rules

Apply these rules when changing files under `fe/`.

## Project Context

- This is a Flutter app named `money_care`.
- Use Dart SDK constraints from `fe/pubspec.yaml`.
- State management and routing are based on GetX.
- The app uses Firebase, `flutter_dotenv`, `get_storage`, `fpdart`, `freezed`, `json_serializable`, `fl_chart`, `flutter_svg`, and `iconsax_flutter`.
- The UI font family is `BeVietnamPro`.

## Architecture

- Keep the existing feature-first Clean Architecture shape:
  - `features/<feature>/data/datasources`
  - `features/<feature>/data/models`
  - `features/<feature>/data/repositories`
  - `features/<feature>/domain/entities`
  - `features/<feature>/domain/repositories`
  - `features/<feature>/domain/usecases`
  - `features/<feature>/presentation/bindings`
  - `features/<feature>/presentation/controllers`
  - `features/<feature>/presentation/screens`
  - `features/<feature>/presentation/widgets`
- Put shared widgets in `lib/app/widgets`.
- Put shared constants, services, networking, errors, storage, theme, and utilities in `lib/core`.
- Do not move feature code into `core` or `app` unless it is genuinely reusable across features.
- Keep domain entities free from Flutter widgets, GetX, HTTP, Firebase, and storage concerns.
- Keep API DTO/model parsing in the data layer, not in screens or controllers.

## State Management and DI

- Use `GetxController` for presentation state and side effects.
- Expose controller state with `.obs`, `Rxn<T>`, or `RxList<T>` following nearby controller style.
- Register dependencies through `Bindings`, `AppBinding`, or feature bindings. Avoid constructing repositories, datasources, or controllers directly inside widgets.
- Use `Get.find<T>()` only where this project already uses service locator access; prefer constructor injection for new controllers and use cases.
- Keep async controller methods explicit about loading, saving, and error states.
- Avoid overlapping requests when existing code already caches a running `Future`.

## Networking and Errors

- Use `core/network/api_client.dart` and `core/constants/api_routes.dart` for backend calls.
- Datasources should throw `ServerException` or another `core/errors/exceptions.dart` exception when API responses fail.
- Repositories should convert exceptions into `Either<Failure, T>` from `fpdart`.
- Use `Right(value)` and `Left(ServerFailure(message))` consistently with existing repositories.
- Do not leak raw API response maps into presentation code. Convert models to domain entities with `toEntity()`.
- Keep JSON parsing tolerant of backend numeric/string differences when adjacent code does so.

## Models and Generated Code

- Prefer `freezed` and `json_serializable` for new immutable DTOs when the surrounding feature uses them.
- Never edit generated files directly: `*.freezed.dart`, `*.g.dart`.
- After changing freezed/json models, run:

```powershell
cd fe
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```

- If a feature uses manual models, match that feature's existing style unless a broader refactor is requested.

## Routing

- Add app routes in `lib/app/router/app_router.dart`.
- Add route names in `lib/core/constants/route_path.dart` when a route is reused or referenced from multiple places.
- Attach feature bindings to `GetPage` entries when the screen needs feature-scoped dependencies.
- Use existing `Transition` patterns for full-screen navigation.

## UI and Widgets

- Match the existing visual system: `AppTheme`, `AppColors`, `AppThemeColors`, `Sizes`, shared app widgets, and `BeVietnamPro`.
- Prefer composing existing widgets from `lib/app/widgets` before creating new one-off UI.
- Keep screens thin: layout and orchestration in screens, reusable pieces in `presentation/widgets`, business logic in controllers/use cases.
- Use `const` constructors wherever possible.
- Do not hardcode repeated spacing, colors, image paths, icon paths, route names, or API paths when a project constant exists.
- Use `flutter_svg`/`AppSvgIcon` for SVG assets and `iconsax_flutter` when icon glyphs are needed.
- Make mobile layouts responsive and avoid fixed heights that can clip Vietnamese text, keyboard overlays, or smaller screens.

## Localization and Text

- The app supports Vietnamese and English through `AppTranslations`.
- Prefer translation keys for new user-facing text when the text belongs to normal product UI.
- Add new keys to both `core/localization/vi_vn.dart` and `core/localization/en_us.dart`.
- Keep backend error fallbacks concise and user-readable.
- Preserve existing Vietnamese copy if only touching unrelated logic.

## Assets and Environment

- Add image/icon assets under `fe/assets/images` or `fe/assets/icons` and declare new asset folders/files in `pubspec.yaml` if needed.
- Do not commit real secrets in `fe/.env`.
- Read backend URLs through `flutter_dotenv` and the existing `API_BASE_URL` / `API_LOCALHOST_URL` pattern.

## Quality Checks

- Before finishing FE changes, run the narrowest useful checks from `fe/`:

```powershell
flutter analyze
flutter test
dart format lib test
```

- If generated models changed, run build_runner before analysis.
- If platform code changed, validate on the affected platform when feasible.
- Report any command that could not be run and why.

## Code Style

- Follow `flutter_lints` and existing local naming.
- Use `package:money_care/...` imports for project code.
- Keep comments rare and useful.
- Keep edits scoped to the requested behavior. Do not refactor unrelated features while implementing a FE task.
